Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Description: Fast equivalents of grepl(), grep(), sub(), gsub() and agrepl()
    that use PCRE2 for regular expressions, prepared literal search and
    Aho-Corasick automata for fixed strings, and Myers' bit-parallel
    algorithm for approximate matching, parallelised across CPU cores via
    Intel TBB through RcppParallel. Also provides match extraction, field
    splitting, whitespace squishing, padding, whole-token dictionary
    replacement, ASCII folding, URL and HTML entity decoding and
    'OpenRefine' clustering keys; parsing numbers from messy text,
    character-class shapes for profiling formats, check-digit validation of
    identifiers (Luhn, ABN, ACN, TFN, Medicare, ISBN, EAN, IBAN) and keyed
    hashing (HMAC with SHA-256, SHA-512, SHA-1 or MD5, and XXH64) for
    pseudonymisation; byte- and Unicode-aware string similarities and edit
    distances (Levenshtein with weights, OSA, Damerau-Levenshtein, LCS,
    Indel, Editex, Smith-Waterman-Gotoh, Monge-Elkan, q-gram set and cosine
    similarity, and edit operations); ports of the 'RapidFuzz'
    fuzzy-matching scorers and search functions
    <https://github.com/rapidfuzz/RapidFuzz>; phonetic blocking keys
    (Soundex, Refined Soundex, NYSIIS, Cologne, Metaphone, Double Metaphone,
    Caverphone, Match Rating Approach, Statistics Canada, Lein, Phonex,
    Roger Root and ONCA); fixed-format date and timestamp parsing; and
    candidate search for record linkage without a full comparison matrix
    (top-N lookup, symmetric-delete search within k edits, TF-IDF n-gram
    cosine matching and MinHash locality-sensitive hashing), multi-pass
    blocking and the sorted neighbourhood method for candidate pairs, and
    connected-component clustering of matched pairs. Includes a
    reproducible benchmark harness for measuring workload- and
    platform-specific performance.
